Z||000000||AL||02-23-2000||08:53 PM||||<BR>today i spotted an se, it was brown and it looked good,even had cheap mudflaps that looked ok, but what caught my eye the most is that this older gentleman that was driving this car put on the deck grilles a fan on each one.they looked like radator fans like in the t a but he installed them on the vents of his car, it didn't look crapy but his idea of doing this made sense, if he has these fans connected to his radiator fan switch, then when the car gets hot those little fans kick in shootin cold air in the engine bay, have any of you seen this? or tried this? if the guy with this car is in this forum please respond. i saw you on the 60 frwy here in california, well guys i just wanted to tell you  what i saw, AL.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||02-23-2000||09:03 PM||||I have a extra radiator fan and I've thought about installing it under the trunk scoop I purchased from Tom which I will be putting on soon, but then I thought, air is supposed to be forced OUT from the bottom, not into the engine bay.||||reg||5
Z||000002||fiero56||02-23-2000||09:46 PM||||When the car is in motion, air is supposed to rise up out of those grills. Drive down the highway 15 minutes and feel the rear glass. It gets very warm just above them, and is normal temp between them. There is a low pressure zone right above them  created by the notchback design(designed for that reason).||||reg||1
